# ShopPilot kanban card sizing

When creating, splitting, or dispatching Hermes kanban tasks for ShopPilot:

## Lanes
- `coder` → Nous Portal `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731`
- `spark` → local Qwen `unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4` @ `:8888`
- **max_in_progress_per_profile = 3** (builds serialized via `swift_locked`; watch exit-124 before going to 4)

## Hardware / throughput reality
- Bottleneck is **parallel `swift build`/`swift test` + fat prompts + epic cards**, not GPU seq count
- 8–16 concurrent agents on one Mac anti-throughput for this repo
- **Fix:** keep 2+2 coding; serialize Swift via `./scripts/swift_locked.sh`

## Card size (mandatory)
One card = **one thin vertical slice**, finishable in **≤45–90 minutes** wall-clock.
Prefer `--max-runtime 45m` or `60m`.

Each card MUST include:
1. Parent SPK id (from `MASTER_KANBAN.md`)
2. **AC** — 1–3 bullets, testable
3. **Out of scope** — explicit
4. **Verify** — one concrete check, prefer in order:
   - `./scripts/verify_locked.sh ShopPilotVerifyXXXX`
   - `scripts/verify_*.py` / standalone
   - `./scripts/swift_locked.sh build --target OneTarget` only if unavoidable
   - **Never** default to full-package `swift build` or bare `swift test` (CLT has no XCTest)
5. workspace **worktree**; assignee `coder` or `spark`
6. Body must require: all swift via `swift_locked.sh`; never `rm -rf .build`; worktree-only Sources edits

## Never put on one card
- Full Engine+UI+Persist+Verify for a whole feature family
- “Productize X stage” / “spine” / “E2E recipe” without splitting
- Multiple unrelated packages (e.g. Serial + Geometry + README)

## Split pattern
Parent `SPK-0XXX` → children `SPK-0XXXa`, `b`, `c`…  

## DoD mapping
Keep product DoD (Engine/UI/Persist/Verify) on the **parent** SPK in `MASTER_KANBAN.md`.  
Micros may close with only the slice’s Verify; parent stays `[ ]` until slices cover DoD.

## Concurrency
At most **3** running per profile (6 total). Serialize cards that edit the same hot files.
One Swift compile at a time via the lock — do not start a second `swift` while waiting.
